Z||000000||HotFieroGT||12-15-1999||02:22 AM||||You guys may remember me talking about a black 88 GT w/5speed I found for $1995.00 on a used car lot in Los Angeles.  I ended up offering him $1000.00 (which he took) because it had problems going into gear (grinding),he just wanted to get rid of car because he didn't want to have to pull the tranny and redo the clutch again.  Well I drove it for a while and decided to check the fluid in the tranny today after I found out there is a dipstick on the Getrag 5-speed.  It wasn't reading on the stick so I decide to pick up a quart of 5W-30 to top it off.  I added a little oil and it still didn't read on the stick, so I kept adding oil until that quart was empty and it still wasn't reading on the stick.  I went and got another quart and it suck down the whole quart again, I was shocked.  This time the stick was reading right where it should.  I got in the car and drove down the street and couldn't believe it, it shifts like butter and the grinding is completely gone!  I can't believe they put a clutch in this car and never checked the trans. fluid.  This just reinforces an old saying I heard a while back, always check the basics first!    <p>[This message has been edited by HotFieroGT (edited 12-15-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||12-15-1999||02:32 AM||||great find!! now we can all debate about what<BR>kind of fluid actually is suppose to go in it. ATF? 5W30? or some kind of synthetic fluid that GM sells for $17.00 per quart. <P>The debate will always continue&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;<P>Congradulations! we are all very jealous.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 12-15-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||12-15-1999||02:48 AM||||We already had that debate.. don't remember when..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  There actually <B>is</B> a special fluid that's supposed to go in it.  go to <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/trans-fluid.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/trans-fluid.html</A> <P>In 88 GM changed thier recommendation from 5w30 to Syncromesh.  $7 a quart.  GM p/n 12345349<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 12-15-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||Sage||12-15-1999||10:52 PM||||Well done HFGT!  Have a friend who would turn green on the spot if I told him of your find.  He has been wanting an 88GT for 4 years but doesn't want to pay what the ones he has located are going for.  Congratulations on your luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
